  "content": {
    "id": "p32-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "A cylindrical piece of ice has a base of radius $4\\text{ cm}$ and a height of $4\\text{ cm}$. This ice is melted, and then refrozen as a cube. Find the side length of this cube.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$4\\sqrt[3]{\\pi}\\text{ cm}$\n\nEquate the cylinder and cube volumes.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}V&=\\pi r^2h\\\\V&=\\pi\\times4^2\\times4\\\\V&=64\\pi\\text{ cm}^3\\end{align*}$$\n\nAfter refreezing, the cube has the original volume. Let its side length be $s\\text{ cm}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}s^3&=64\\pi\\\\s&=\\sqrt[3]{64\\pi}\\\\s&=4\\sqrt[3]{\\pi}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe side length is $4\\sqrt[3]{\\pi}\\text{ cm}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 68
  },
